 "findings": [
  "All acceptance terms still pass: 15,150,646 bytes accepted, 449 pictures, 448 swaps, sequence end, presentation complete, terminal reason 1 (quiet), error_flags 0, no cache-bank overlap, no presentation error, no audio underrun, no PCM protocol error, no timestamp conflicts.",
  "The entry 567 hypothesis is refuted. The cold first run after a full reboot does not run clean; it produces the largest gap measured so far.",
  "The single outlier is again at display picture ordinal 6, but is 6,006,000 cycles (100.1 ms) - three nominal intervals, versus two in both warm runs.",
  "input_starved_cycles_since_previous_swap at ordinal 6 rises to 1,659,347 (27.66 ms) from approximately 1,072,000 (17.85 ms) in the warm runs, a 55 percent increase.",
  "accepted_bytes_at_deadline falls to 296,838 from 323,580 and 331,179, so fewer bytes had been delivered by the same deadline - the upstream feed is measurably slower when cold.",
  "candidate_ready_delay_cycles rises to 3,230,418 from 592,128 and 271,690.",
  "Writer and DDR remain clean in every run: upstream_fifo_pending, writer_busy and writer_capacity_blocked all false with zero capacity-blocked cycles.",
  "The starvation magnitude tracks how cold the source is, which is consistent with ARM-side file read latency at startup rather than with session rearm state.",
  "presentation_hold_total_cycles is the lowest of all four runs at 26,390,166, so the guarded startup wait did not lengthen to compensate; the guard released on readiness while the feed was still behind.",
  "Ranked gaps 2 and 3 remain exactly 2,002,000 cycles, so steady-state cadence after the startup hitch is nominal in every run measured."
 ],
 "scope_limitations": [
